               <msContents>
                  <summary><hi rend="italic">Yotserot</hi> in the Ashkenazic rite, for the whole
                     year</summary>
                  <msItem>
                     <title type="desc" xml:lang="he" key="work_3377">יוצרות מנהג אשכנז לכל
                        השנה</title>
                     <title type="desc" xml:lang="he-Latn-x-lc" key="work_3377">Yotserot minhag
                        Ashkenaz le-khol ha-shanah</title>
                     <note>The final portion of the manuscript contains <hi rend="italic"
                           >reshuyot</hi> and <hi rend="italic">zemirot</hi> in honour of the
                        bridegroom. The end of the manuscript is defective.</note>
                     <note>Most of the <hi rend="italic">piyyutim</hi> are headed with the authors'
                        names added by a later hand; authors to whom the <hi rend="italic"
                           >piyyutim</hi> have been attributed include <persName key="person_7086"
                           >Ḥayyim Palṭiʾel <foreign xml:lang="he">חיים פלטיאל</foreign></persName>,
                           <persName key="person_7087">Meʾir Mesoli (?)<foreign xml:lang="he">מאיר
                              מסולי</foreign></persName>, <persName key="person_7088">Shmuʾel of
                           Meyerburg (?)<foreign xml:lang="he">שמואל ממיירבורק
                        </foreign></persName>, and <persName key="person_7089">Shmuʾel Kohen
                              <foreign xml:lang="he">שמואל כהן</foreign></persName>.</note>
                     <note>Some of the <hi rend="italic">piyyutim</hi> are accompanied by a
                        commentary on the margin, which is largely of a grammatical nature. The
                        commentary is probably by a scholar from Bohemia; he cited words '<foreign
                           xml:lang="he">בלשון כנען</foreign>' ('in the language of Canaan', here
                        referring to a Slavic language) (see for example <locus>f.
                        17v</locus>).</note>
                     <note>Authors quoted in the commentary include <persName key="person_90489505"
                           >Solomon ibn Parḥon <foreign xml:lang="he">שלמה יבן
                           פרחון</foreign></persName>, <persName key="person_90633023">Abraham ibn
                           Ezra <foreign xml:lang="he">אברהם יבן עזרא</foreign></persName>,
                           <persName key="person_7085">Mosheh ha-Sefardi <foreign xml:lang="he">משה
                              הספרדי</foreign></persName>, and one '<persName>Rabbi Eliʿezer
                              <foreign xml:lang="he">הר׳ אליעזר</foreign></persName>'.</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="he">Hebrew</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
